The 256-row test measured 159.46 s for the monolithic 48-boundary route. Adjacent-interval recombination was close but not bit-identical for batched rows, so I will not use it for strict decisions. The implementation will use the sealed monolithic path, parallelize only independent anchors (maximum four), and checkpoint the completed scan before the much costlier convergence follow-up.
